load @/code/structure/manifold
  find manifold

# The hyperbolic plane: the two-dimensional space of constant negative curvature, the third geometry beside the sphere
# and the flat plane. In it the angles of a triangle sum to less than two right angles, the deficit measuring the area,
# parallel lines diverge, and the circumference of a circle grows exponentially with its radius. There is always more
# room than in flat space, which is exactly the room the mesh needs to grow shell by shell without crowding. The form
# carries the underlying manifold; constant negative curvature is the defining condition.
form hyperbolic-plane
  link manifold, like manifold
